# Unauth direction

Treat `docs/PRODUCT.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, and `CLAUDE.md` as the maintained product and engineering contract.

Unauth is a source-agnostic post-purchase payout-control, loss, and recovery platform. Commerce, helpdesk, fulfillment, payment, and import providers feed one merchant-scoped model and timeline.

Use neutral operational language: payout exposure, support payout case, evidence strength, merchant rule, recommended action, loss attribution, recoverability, recovery owner, prevention opportunity, policy leakage, and partner accountability.

Do not present Unauth as an accusation engine. Merchant rules make explainable recommendations; the merchant controls and records the final outcome.

Keep helpdesk widgets compressed. Full investigation belongs on the Unauth case page; recovery operations belong in Recovery; provider-specific setup belongs in Integrations.

New providers extend shared canonical and connector contracts instead of creating parallel product models.
